        "reviewed_notes": "Franco took office as head of the Nationalist Spanish State on 1 October 1936 following Decree 138 of 29 September. The 1936–1939 interval denotes authority within Nationalist-held territory, not control of the entire country. The Congress of Deputies dates the post-Civil War regime to April 1939; the same head of state remained in office until his death on 20 November 1975. Preserve the existing Spanish State identity and role.",
